<markdown_cell>
## Common errors

- **`stub` not found:** bats-core v1.14.0 provides `stub` and `unstub` as built-in helpers loaded via `load stub`. If `stub` is undefined, ensure `load stub` appears in the test file or `setup.bash` before any `@test` block.
- **Stale stubs between tests:** Each test runs in its own subshell in bats-core. Stubs set in one test do not leak to others, but `setup_file` runs once per file — define stub cleanup there if a test file shares state.
- **`PATH` prefix not exported:** The fake `PATH` containing stub executables must be exported (`export PATH="$STUBDIR:$PATH"`) so that child processes of the script under test also resolve the stubs.
- **`gzip` stub returns wrong code:** `gzip` must return 0 on success for rotation tests to pass. A stub that always returns 1 will cause every rotation test to fail silently — verify stub return codes match real behavior.
- **`set -e` in tested scripts swallowing stubs:** If the script under test uses `set -e`, a stub returning non-zero will abort the script before assertions run. Guard stubbed commands with `|| true` or use `set +e` in the test scope.
</markdown_cell>

